Package: rgrc
Architecture: amd64 arm64 armhf i386
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: Rusty Generic Colouriser, a fast grc written in Rust
 rgrc colorizes the output of other commands such as ping, df, ls, ps,
 docker, journalctl, kubectl, dig, ip and netstat using grc/grcat-style
 configuration files. It runs a command and colors its output
 (rgrc ping -c 4 debian.org) or colors piped input (df -h | rgrc -c df).
 .
 Ships around 100 command configs in /usr/share/rgrc, the main mapping in
 /etc/rgrc.conf, and completions for bash, fish and zsh. Aliases are not
 enabled by default; add eval "$(rgrc --aliases)" to your shell rc file.
